      "solution": "$\\int_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} (\\sin 3x + 5\\cos x)\\,dx = \\left[-\\frac{1}{3}\\cos 3x + 5\\sin x\\right]_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} = \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cos\\frac{3\\pi}{2} + 5\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) - \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cos 0 + 5\\sin 0\\right) = 0 + 5 - \\left(-\\frac{1}{3} + 0\\right) = 5 + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{16}{3}$",
